# Generating a rule for a named copy
#
# A source has a value and a named copy. An N3 rule generates a backward
# rule that exposes the source's value through the copy, showing a bound
# name carried into a new rule.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/issue118/issue118.n3> .
@prefix : <http:/example.org/> .
@prefix skolem: <https://eyereasoner.github.io/.well-known/genid/d983461b-11b7-4e52-89c1-328e91bf1de1#> .

# The copy already has a supplied IRI; this rule does not invent its name.
:s :value 1 .
:s :copy skolem:bn_5 .

# Any subject whose value can be found is classified as a Success.
{
    ?s :value ?value
} => {
    ?s a :Success
} .

# Capture the copy IRI in a backward rule that reads the source value.
# That new definition also lets the Success rule recognize the copy.
{
    :s :copy ?o
} => {
    {
        ?o :value ?value
    } <= {
        :s :value ?value
    }
} .
